     I am not going to bore you all with the details of what was (I
think) a relatively boring ascension.  I was chipping away at the
dungeon with a neutral caveman for some time with little luck
(actually, I posted recently about another caveman getting worked
unexpectedly by the Chromatic Dragon- this was 2 cavemen later), when
the ice suddenly broke.  I can't remember exactly what happened, but it
involved switching from a +1 club to mojo (didn't find an altar until
about DLVL20).  Soon after i found awand of wishing in the VoD.
Suddenly I was sitting on a buttload of wishes.  Even better, I found a
lot of my ascention kit just lying around before I even got around to
using the wishes.
     By the time I was done I had used 10 wishes, genocided 37 species
and died three times.  That being said, I must add that a lot of that
was done on the planes which I reached for the first time this game
(Rodney always got me before- stupid double trouble).  I died not once,
not twice but thrice on the plane of air (Archons can be an
indescribable pain for those who have never been there before).  On
both the plane of air and the plane of fire I ended up surrounded on
all sides (about 5 layers deep) by badasses.  I am playing on a cpu
with a dying monitor so I couldnt even tell the difference between the
little number 3's (fire elementals warning number) and the waves of
lava.  I cant really recall how I managed to survive and find the
portals, except that I know it involved very elegant and artful use of
my amulets of life saving- including wishing for new ones as needed- as
well as a desperation genocide of D when I thought there was absolutely
no escape.  Only after reading this scroll did I realize that I was
confused (nearly cried when I thougt I lost my first near-ascension so
close to the end).  Somehow, it did not send in dragons and the
genocide worked.  Any idea why?  I will, never, EVER try to go to the
planes wihtout being 100% sure I have a way of finding those portals
first.  The astral plane was a comparative breeze, and thus I ascended
to demigod-hood for the first time along with my pet Mastodon (fitting
for a caveman) El Duderino (not into the whole brevity thing).

There you have it-  I don't know why I posted, I guess just to let you
all know that there is one more in your ranks.  There are many vices in
this world, I am glad Nethack is mine- er, one  of mine.

It seems to me that the early game and Gehennom get far more attention
than the planes do- many spoilers and faqs give them just a few lines,
when they deserve pages (probably just my inexperience talking).  There
is a demogorgon FAQ butnothing about dealing with Archons.  Just
curious...

